---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import headshot from '../assets/photos/aaron-amerling.jpg';
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About — Aaron Amerling"
			description="Growth marketing leader with a background in storytelling, product, and applied AI."
		/>
		<style>
			.about-hero {
				display: flex;
				align-items: center;
				gap: 2em;
				margin-bottom: 1em;
			}
			.about-hero :global(img) {
				width: 120px;
				height: 120px;
				object-fit: cover;
				border-radius: 999px;
				flex-shrink: 0;
			}
			main {
				width: 720px;
				max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
				margin: auto;
				padding: 3em 1em;
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
			}
			h2 {
				color: rgb(var(--black));
				margin-top: 1.75em;
			}
			ul {
				padding-left: 1.2em;
			}
			li {
				margin-bottom: 0.4em;
			}
			@media (max-width: 560px) {
				.about-hero {
					flex-direction: column;
					text-align: center;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="about-hero">
				<div class="avatar-ring">
					<Image src={headshot} alt="Aaron Amerling" width={120} height={120} />
				</div>
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
					<h1>Aaron Amerling</h1>
				</div>
			</div>

			<p>
				I'm a growth marketing leader who owns the number, not just the channel. I build
				measurable, trackable pipeline across B2B and B2B2C audiences, run the full digital and
				revenue-operations stack, and do it AI-natively — deploying Generative Engine Optimization
				(GEO) and Answer Engine Optimization (AEO) as live growth channels ahead of the category,
				and rolling generative AI workflows across marketing organizations. My background spans
				regulated financial services marketing, lean high-output teams, and hands-on execution
				alongside team leadership.
			</p>

			<p>
				Most recently I was Head of Marketing / CMO at Etna Interactive, where I led a
				60-person organization spanning paid, owned, earned, strategy and client services. Before
				that, as VP of Strategy at The Lemonade Agency, I oversaw marketing for clients including
				Disney, Meta, Square Enix, Ubisoft, Dior and DirecTV. Earlier in my career I managed a
				$40M+ digital marketing budget at GAIN Credit and built GreatCall's (now Best Buy Health)
				first direct-to-consumer digital strategy — helping grow mobile users from 25,000 to over
				1.5 million.
			</p>

			<p>
				I started as a writer — credits include Nickelodeon's <em>Avatar: The Last Airbender</em>,
				a 20th Century Fox New Writers Award, and a Nickelodeon Fellowship. That instinct for
				narrative is still where I start: it's why I was able to reverse years of decline for the
				San Francisco Marathon through repositioning, and why I care as much about the story a
				brand tells as the channel mechanics underneath it.
			</p>

			<h2>Applied AI</h2>
			<p>
				I stood up Answer Engine Optimization as a growth channel before most agencies had a name
				for it, and I design, prototype and ship with AI tooling myself rather than just briefing
				it out. I mentor early-stage AI founders through Techstars, and as a strategic advisor to
				Steno.ai I identified the digital-cloning use case that landed Tony Robbins as the
				company's flagship customer. I was also an early marketing advisor to GoFundMe, back when
				it was three people around a table and still called "Create-A-Fund."
			</p>

			<h2>Patents & recognition</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Co-inventor, five U.S. patents for a trust-network architecture — originally built for
					emergency response call centers and written broadly enough to cover authentication,
					identity verification, and influence targeting; assigned to GreatCall / Best Buy Health.
				</li>
				<li>Runner-up, CONNECT Most Innovative Product of the Year (Mobile Apps)</li>
				<li>International Communicator Award; three International Telly Awards, Digital Advertising</li>
				<li>Nickelodeon Fellowship Recipient; 20th Century Fox New Writers Award</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Education</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>M.A. in Digital Media, TV and Film — San Diego State University</li>
				<li>B.A. in History — University of California, Santa Cruz</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>FAQ</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Has he worked on AI products, or only AI in marketing?</strong><br />
				Both. As a strategic advisor to Steno.ai, a Techstars '23 AI digital-twin company, he
				identified the use case for digital cloning in the expert and influencer markets and led
				the engagement that secured Tony Robbins as the flagship customer. He also mentors
				early-stage AI founders through the Techstars network, and launched AI consumer-facing
				products while Chief Marketing Officer at Etna Interactive.
			</p>

			<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/aaronamerling/">LinkedIn</a></li>
				<li><a href="mailto:aaronamerling@gmail.com">aaronamerling@gmail.com</a></li>
			</ul>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
